1
00:00:00,156 --> 00:00:02,156
(A Bona fide Killer)

2
00:00:07,847 --> 00:00:09,670
(This drama, its characters,
and events are fictional.)

3
00:00:09,694 --> 00:00:10,843
(Scenes with child actors
and animals were supervised.)

4
00:00:10,855 --> 00:00:11,890
(Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency)

5
00:00:11,890 --> 00:00:13,825
(Episode 11)

6
00:00:14,526 --> 00:00:17,228
(Police)

7
00:00:17,262 --> 00:00:19,998
(Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency)

8
00:00:23,735 --> 00:00:25,236
I'm coming with you.

9
00:00:28,973 --> 00:00:31,209
I told you to stay put
and learn from your new superior.

10
00:00:31,609 --> 00:00:33,077
You're just asking for trouble.

11
00:00:33,077 --> 00:00:36,247
Where you go, I go.
What would you do without me?

12
00:00:39,384 --> 00:00:41,819
- Are you ready for this?
- I was born ready.

13
00:00:43,054 --> 00:00:44,322
Keep your voice down.

14
00:00:47,025 --> 00:00:48,493
Let's go.

15
00:00:48,960 --> 00:00:50,662
- To catch Kingfisher.
- Yes.

16
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,634
Dong Jin!

17
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:01,773
A Special
Investigation Team aimed at arresting...

18
00:01:01,773 --> 00:01:03,641
the serial killer Kingfisher...

19
00:01:03,675 --> 00:01:06,611
was launched today
at the Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency.

20
00:01:06,611 --> 00:01:08,313
This Special Investigation Team

21
00:01:08,313 --> 00:01:09,614
is different from the ones before.

22
00:01:09,647 --> 00:01:12,250
It won't be created for show
and then quietly disbanded.

23
00:01:12,250 --> 00:01:13,518
That will absolutely not happen.

24
00:01:13,551 --> 00:01:15,954
This time, we are determined
to see this through to the end...

25
00:01:15,954 --> 00:01:17,989
and will pour all our resources into it.

26
00:01:17,989 --> 00:01:21,359
Is this the third time they've pledged
all available resources?

27
00:01:21,392 --> 00:01:22,594
No. It's the fourth.

28
00:01:23,261 --> 00:01:27,031
They probably created and disbanded one
every 3 or 4 years.

29
00:01:27,031 --> 00:01:28,800
I wonder what "the end" will be this time.

30
00:01:29,334 --> 00:01:30,335
That is all.

31
00:01:31,536 --> 00:01:32,904
("Re-Examining Past Cases
Using Latest Techniques")

32
00:01:39,544 --> 00:01:42,280
Now, this is a profiler
from the Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency,

33
00:01:42,280 --> 00:01:44,048
Inspector Yu Mi Ran.

34
00:01:44,082 --> 00:01:45,083
(Kingfisher Special Investigation Team)

35
00:01:45,083 --> 00:01:46,451
(Yu Mi Ran)

36
00:01:47,085 --> 00:01:48,186
I'm sure you all know her, right?

37
00:01:48,219 --> 00:01:50,288
She solved the Oseong-gu
serial murder case...

38
00:01:50,288 --> 00:01:51,556
that was cold for 20 years.

39
00:01:51,823 --> 00:01:53,892
A celebrity in the police world,
you could say?

40
00:01:56,861 --> 00:01:58,062
I applied because they said
there's no overtime...

41
00:01:58,062 --> 00:01:59,998
and weekends are guaranteed.

42
00:02:01,399 --> 00:02:03,201
- That's right, isn't it?
- Really?

43
00:02:03,234 --> 00:02:04,669
It isn't?

44
00:02:04,669 --> 00:02:05,770
Then I shouldn't have.

45
00:02:06,237 --> 00:02:07,305
Maybe I should just go back.

46
00:02:08,373 --> 00:02:10,842
All right,
now that we've all been introduced,

47
00:02:10,875 --> 00:02:12,143
let's get down to business.

48
00:02:12,143 --> 00:02:13,378
(Controversy Over Kingfisher Suspects)

49
00:02:18,383 --> 00:02:21,052
No matter how I think about it,
I just don't understand.

50
00:02:23,154 --> 00:02:24,522
If you look at it one way,

51
00:02:24,522 --> 00:02:27,392
didn't Kingfisher get revenge for him
on his parents' killer?

52
00:02:28,393 --> 00:02:31,162
For him to try and catch that very person
with his own hands...

53
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:33,731
Even if he is a cop.

54
00:02:34,799 --> 00:02:37,669
Do you see your job
as enacting someone else's revenge?

55
00:02:37,669 --> 00:02:39,103
No, it's not like that, but...

56
00:02:40,538 --> 00:02:43,975
Everyone just chooses their own path
for their own reasons.

57
00:02:44,676 --> 00:02:48,112
Some people can't become like us.

58
00:02:48,680 --> 00:02:50,548
And we just have to do our job.

59
00:02:51,549 --> 00:02:52,550
Right?

60
00:02:53,918 --> 00:02:54,919
Here you are.

61
00:02:57,922 --> 00:02:59,224
It's 12 p.m. Let's get lunch.

62
00:02:59,924 --> 00:03:01,125
Really?

63
00:03:01,559 --> 00:03:05,396
Hey, so what should we get
for lunch today?

64
00:03:06,431 --> 00:03:10,101
- Gosh, look at the time.
- Lunchtime.

65
00:03:10,835 --> 00:03:12,337
It's hot out. How about some cold noodles?

66
00:03:12,937 --> 00:03:14,539
- Cold noodles sound great. Let's go.
- Sounds good.

67
00:03:14,539 --> 00:03:16,174
- Hey, Ko, let's go.
- Yes.

68
00:03:16,207 --> 00:03:17,609
I'm getting the cold noodles with broth.

69
00:03:21,646 --> 00:03:23,948
I wonder if Manager Tae Min
will just grab something quick again.

70
00:03:25,850 --> 00:03:27,986
I wonder if he can eat
in a place like that.

71
00:03:28,019 --> 00:03:30,121
Don't worry. He'll manage for now.

72
00:03:30,788 --> 00:03:32,423
What? For now?

73
00:03:32,957 --> 00:03:33,958
Why?

74
00:04:23,875 --> 00:04:24,976
Kingfisher...

75
00:04:25,443 --> 00:04:29,047
is a systematic killer who acts
with clear motives and objectives.

76
00:04:29,914 --> 00:04:33,818
His weapon of choice is a sniper rifle,
which is hard for civilians to obtain.

77
00:04:34,385 --> 00:04:35,453
Given the circumstances,

78
00:04:35,453 --> 00:04:39,357
we should start by assuming
he has superior physical abilities, right?

79
00:04:39,357 --> 00:04:43,027
So, wouldn't someone from a military
special forces unit be the most likely?

80
00:04:43,061 --> 00:04:47,665
I've already investigated that sector.
Before Kingfisher first appeared in 2010,

81
00:04:47,699 --> 00:04:49,934
I looked into veterans
from military special forces units.

82
00:04:49,968 --> 00:04:52,403
I narrowed it down to 400 people
with outstanding marksmanship...

83
00:04:52,403 --> 00:04:53,404
and investigated each one,

84
00:04:54,339 --> 00:04:56,007
but I couldn't find any credible suspects.

85
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:58,710
So you were basically looking for a needle
in a haystack.

86
00:05:01,012 --> 00:05:02,747
If they completed their service
in the special forces,

87
00:05:03,081 --> 00:05:05,516
then all 400 of them must have been
adult South Korean men, right?

88
00:05:07,552 --> 00:05:09,687
Yes. I would assume so.

89
00:05:10,855 --> 00:05:14,559
So, are you saying
Kingfisher could be a woman or a minor?

90
00:05:15,727 --> 00:05:16,794
What is this, a movie?

91
00:05:20,231 --> 00:05:24,335
Instead of being trapped by the bias
that the suspect is an adult Korean man,

92
00:05:24,335 --> 00:05:26,070
we should keep all possibilities open.

93
00:05:26,671 --> 00:05:29,574
Gender, age, nationality, and so on.

94
00:05:31,209 --> 00:05:32,544
<i>Kingfisher is...</i>

95
00:05:33,478 --> 00:05:34,746
a tall,

96
00:05:36,347 --> 00:05:37,849
well-built,

97
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:40,552
young man.

98
00:05:42,153 --> 00:05:44,589
And there's one more thing
we need to pay attention to.

99
00:05:44,622 --> 00:05:45,957
(Analysis of Inactive Periods)

100
00:05:45,957 --> 00:05:46,958
The inactive periods.

101
00:05:48,293 --> 00:05:51,162
Are you talking
about the Haegong-dong Gosiwon Case?

102
00:05:51,196 --> 00:05:53,164
Exactly.

103
00:05:53,765 --> 00:05:56,401
He was inactive for four years after that.

104
00:05:56,935 --> 00:06:00,438
A serial killer's inactive period
is usually explained in two ways.

105
00:06:00,471 --> 00:06:03,841
One is external control,
such as being arrested or imprisoned.

106
00:06:04,642 --> 00:06:06,411
The other is internal saturation.

107
00:06:07,312 --> 00:06:09,047
In other words, the impulse subsides...

108
00:06:09,047 --> 00:06:12,217
because their desire has been
temporarily satisfied.

109
00:06:13,685 --> 00:06:16,888
But I think Kingfisher might be different.

110
00:06:17,755 --> 00:06:18,957
Why?

111
00:06:18,957 --> 00:06:24,329
Because Kingfisher isn't
a typical psychopath.

112
00:06:25,997 --> 00:06:28,233
Are you suggesting there's a possibility
of a change of heart or...

113
00:06:28,233 --> 00:06:31,402
a change in his environment?

114
00:06:31,402 --> 00:06:32,637
Exactly.

115
00:06:33,004 --> 00:06:35,039
(Analysis of Inactive Periods)

116
00:06:35,039 --> 00:06:36,875
Besides Haegong-dong,
there's another case.

117
00:06:36,908 --> 00:06:39,277
The so-called World Cup case
from eight years ago.

118
00:06:39,944 --> 00:06:42,013
There was a nine-month gap after that too.

119
00:06:42,413 --> 00:06:43,848
Considering his longest interval
between crimes...

120
00:06:43,848 --> 00:06:48,520
was two months before that,
that's definitely a significant number.

121
00:06:48,953 --> 00:06:52,624
Now, I believe these two gaps,
long and short,

122
00:06:53,591 --> 00:06:57,462
will be the clue that helps us get closer
to Kingfisher's true identity.

123
00:06:59,797 --> 00:07:02,166
Okay. For now, like Inspector Yu said,

124
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:05,436
let's consider the possibility that
a woman or a minor can be the culprit.

125
00:07:05,537 --> 00:07:07,171
First, the World Cup
and Haegong-dong cases.

126
00:07:07,205 --> 00:07:09,507
Let's start by finding the commonalities
between these two cases.

127
00:07:09,507 --> 00:07:12,143
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

128
00:07:15,380 --> 00:07:17,148
<i>The World Cup and Haegong-dong.</i>

129
00:07:17,181 --> 00:07:19,851
You were there for both major incidents.

130
00:07:19,884 --> 00:07:21,186
Statistically,
that doesn't make any sense.

131
00:07:21,219 --> 00:07:22,921
I'm a reporter, you psycho.

132
00:07:25,924 --> 00:07:27,926
(Special Investigation Team)

133
00:07:30,662 --> 00:07:33,364
- Hey, find me those files.
- I'll get right on it.

134
00:07:34,098 --> 00:07:37,268
Inspector Yu, find this file
and send it to our contact.

135
00:07:37,769 --> 00:07:39,204
<i>I heard your reporter friend woke up.</i>

136
00:07:39,637 --> 00:07:40,672
That's a relief.

137
00:07:40,705 --> 00:07:43,074
He had a close brush with death.

138
00:07:43,074 --> 00:07:45,009
Did they find the person
who saved his life?

139
00:07:45,543 --> 00:07:48,146
- The person who called 911.
- The woman.

140
00:07:48,146 --> 00:07:51,149
They said it's hard to identify her
because she called from my friend's phone.

141
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:59,958
But that's the building
where Kingfisher carried out his attack,

142
00:08:00,458 --> 00:08:02,026
and the time is roughly the same.

143
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:07,332
So I'm wondering if maybe Kingfisher
was the one who called it in.

144
00:08:08,666 --> 00:08:12,270
He killed someone upstairs,
then saved someone on his way down?

145
00:08:12,871 --> 00:08:14,372
And it was a woman?

146
00:08:14,739 --> 00:08:16,241
Yes.

147
00:08:16,274 --> 00:08:17,275
Darn it.

148
00:08:17,809 --> 00:08:19,043
Instead of going on a wild goose chase
for someone else's case,

149
00:08:19,043 --> 00:08:20,645
focus on your own, you punk.

150
00:08:30,889 --> 00:08:32,557
(Cheongmok-dong Redevelopment Area
Sniper Case)

151
00:08:33,958 --> 00:08:35,226
(Citymania Hotel Case)

152
00:08:38,863 --> 00:08:40,665
(Incident Report)

153
00:08:43,034 --> 00:08:44,969
(Name of Witness: Hong Seok Woo)

154
00:08:47,539 --> 00:08:51,809
<i>I realized later</i>
<i>that all the CCTV cameras were broken.</i>

155
00:08:52,343 --> 00:08:53,478
I didn't know while I was on duty.

156
00:08:53,978 --> 00:08:56,581
The monitors looked like
they were working just fine.

157
00:08:56,614 --> 00:08:59,584
Was there no one in the building at all?
Like the cleaning crew or anyone.

158
00:09:00,285 --> 00:09:01,686
That day,

159
00:09:02,453 --> 00:09:07,058
there were no employees working late,
and the cleaning ladies left early too.

160
00:09:07,058 --> 00:09:09,027
<i>They wanted to leave</i>
<i>before the crowds gathered for the game.</i>

161
00:09:09,694 --> 00:09:11,196
<i>So it wasn't an employee or a cleaner.</i>

162
00:09:12,297 --> 00:09:13,331
<i>Then who was it?</i>

163
00:09:14,065 --> 00:09:15,600
<i>Who reported Tae Sung?</i>

164
00:09:16,834 --> 00:09:18,937
Kwon Se Ah is always busy.

165
00:09:26,411 --> 00:09:28,913
- What are you looking for?
- It's not here.

166
00:09:28,913 --> 00:09:30,615
The records related to Tae Sung's case.

167
00:09:30,982 --> 00:09:31,983
Tae Sung?

168
00:09:33,084 --> 00:09:34,552
You mean the case where he got mugged...

169
00:09:34,552 --> 00:09:36,354
while chasing a pickpocket
during the World Cup?

170
00:09:36,788 --> 00:09:39,157
Why would that be in there?
That's not even a Kingfisher case.

171
00:09:40,058 --> 00:09:42,360
I wonder if those are two separate cases.

172
00:09:43,061 --> 00:09:44,095
Or what?

173
00:09:53,304 --> 00:09:55,073
- Where are you going?
- Prison.

174
00:09:55,506 --> 00:09:59,043
- You can come if you want.
- What? Why prison? Who's there?

175
00:09:59,043 --> 00:10:01,212
The person who was overlooked
during the investigation.

176
00:10:01,212 --> 00:10:02,714
Who is that?

177
00:10:14,225 --> 00:10:15,994
(Green Sky Welfare Center)

178
00:10:18,329 --> 00:10:21,666
His grandson?
You mean the boy who has trouble speaking?

179
00:10:21,666 --> 00:10:25,403
Yes. The kid's been pretty troubled
ever since what happened to his dad.

180
00:10:25,403 --> 00:10:27,705
Excuse me, do you happen to know
where the boy is now?

181
00:10:27,739 --> 00:10:29,641
Didn't they say he went to some facility?

182
00:10:29,641 --> 00:10:33,678
Yes. He had no one to look after him,
so I think he went to an orphanage.

183
00:10:38,650 --> 00:10:40,818
- You said you were here to see Cheol?
- Yes.

184
00:10:42,086 --> 00:10:44,055
That's him over there.

185
00:10:51,329 --> 00:10:54,299
When he first came,
he had trouble expressing himself,

186
00:10:54,299 --> 00:10:57,936
and he struggled to interact with people.
But he's brightened up a lot now.

187
00:10:58,303 --> 00:10:59,437
That's a relief.

188
00:10:59,938 --> 00:11:01,739
It looks like he enjoys drawing.

189
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:05,643
His sponsor sends him flowers every week,

190
00:11:05,643 --> 00:11:08,012
and on those days,
he always draws them, just like that.

191
00:11:08,446 --> 00:11:09,781
A sponsor?

192
00:11:09,781 --> 00:11:12,617
Someone who supports
various therapy programs for Cheol.

193
00:11:12,650 --> 00:11:14,452
He has an anonymous sponsor.

194
00:11:16,721 --> 00:11:18,957
What's their relationship to the boy?

195
00:11:19,390 --> 00:11:21,726
Well, I'm not really sure about that...

196
00:11:24,996 --> 00:11:26,030
By any chance,

197
00:11:26,464 --> 00:11:29,467
if it's not too much to ask,
could I possibly meet them?

198
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:33,271
I'm afraid that's not possible.
They don't wish to reveal their identity.

199
00:11:35,173 --> 00:11:36,174
I see.

200
00:11:40,812 --> 00:11:42,513
When they send flowers,

201
00:11:43,047 --> 00:11:45,884
they always include a card
with the flower's meaning.

202
00:11:46,851 --> 00:11:50,288
The very first time, there was a separate
message card included,

203
00:11:51,322 --> 00:11:54,559
"I hope you find
your own beautiful scenery."

204
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:55,927
It was just one line written on it.

205
00:12:01,332 --> 00:12:02,834
What did you just say?

206
00:12:03,635 --> 00:12:06,004
- I'm sorry?
- The message on the first card...

207
00:12:06,538 --> 00:12:09,674
"I hope you find your own
beautiful scenery," you mean that one?

208
00:12:11,976 --> 00:12:13,711
<i>I think that's the power of scenery.</i>

209
00:12:14,212 --> 00:12:15,847
Your own special scenery that
gives you energy when you're exhausted...

210
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:19,884
and that helps you get going again
when you've stopped.

211
00:12:19,884 --> 00:12:21,719
Bo Na, have you ever had
a beautiful scenery...

212
00:12:21,719 --> 00:12:22,720
like that in your life?

213
00:12:28,927 --> 00:12:29,994
I'm sorry.

214
00:12:31,029 --> 00:12:32,297
That's a really beautiful thing to say.

215
00:12:34,332 --> 00:12:37,001
They must definitely
have such a romantic vibe.

216
00:12:37,001 --> 00:12:39,304
I agree.

217
00:12:39,304 --> 00:12:42,173
But their tone is so blunt, like a man's.

218
00:12:57,021 --> 00:12:59,858
(Ok's Flower Shop)

219
00:13:03,561 --> 00:13:07,465
So the pickpocket wasn't
caught until a year later.

220
00:13:08,299 --> 00:13:10,702
Then why is he still in here?

221
00:13:10,702 --> 00:13:13,204
Because robbery, assault, and fleeing
were added to his charges.

222
00:13:20,011 --> 00:13:21,412
Looks like prison food agrees with you.

223
00:13:21,746 --> 00:13:22,947
You look healthy.

224
00:13:28,286 --> 00:13:29,387
It's been a while.

225
00:13:29,387 --> 00:13:31,689
Why are you here after all this time?

226
00:13:32,624 --> 00:13:34,492
What, are you here to grab me
by the collar again?

227
00:13:37,996 --> 00:13:39,864
Your friend is alive and well.

228
00:13:40,198 --> 00:13:41,933
Yes, he's alive and well.

229
00:13:42,634 --> 00:13:45,703
I'm here to ask you something today.
About the day you mugged him.

230
00:13:45,770 --> 00:13:48,673
I told you everything back then.
What else is there to say?

231
00:13:53,044 --> 00:13:54,879
Your friend kept chasing me,

232
00:13:54,913 --> 00:13:57,415
so I hit him with a fire extinguisher
to try and knock him out,

233
00:13:58,883 --> 00:14:00,418
but I ended up hitting him too hard.

234
00:14:00,418 --> 00:14:02,086
I know all that.
Tell me what happened after.

235
00:14:02,921 --> 00:14:04,389
After you hit him.

236
00:14:04,389 --> 00:14:07,825
- And then I ran outside.
- You left through the first-floor lobby?

237
00:14:07,825 --> 00:14:09,861
Of course I went out the first floor.
Where else would I go?

238
00:14:09,861 --> 00:14:12,463
Did you see anyone else on your way out?

239
00:14:13,198 --> 00:14:14,332
See anyone?

240
00:14:15,266 --> 00:14:16,467
It was pitch black and totally empty.

241
00:14:19,370 --> 00:14:20,371
Wait a minute.

242
00:14:21,039 --> 00:14:24,475
Come to think of it,
I think there was someone there.

243
00:14:25,810 --> 00:14:26,811
There was?

244
00:14:28,046 --> 00:14:31,849
- Who was it?
- But can I say I saw that?

245
00:14:31,849 --> 00:14:34,719
- It wasn't inside the building...
- Inside or out, who was it?

246
00:14:34,719 --> 00:14:36,187
The person you saw that day.

247
00:14:37,188 --> 00:14:38,323
It was a woman.

248
00:14:51,269 --> 00:14:54,005
<i>At the very moment</i>
<i>Tae Sung chased the pickpocket...</i>

249
00:14:54,005 --> 00:14:55,039
<i>into King Tower...</i>

250
00:14:57,008 --> 00:15:00,278
<i>Kingfisher was on the rooftop</i>
<i>of that building.</i>

251
00:15:21,866 --> 00:15:23,101
<i>At the time,</i>
<i>the victim was on the phone...</i>

252
00:15:23,101 --> 00:15:24,903
<i>with a friend in the hotel</i>
<i>across the street.</i>

253
00:15:24,903 --> 00:15:26,871
- What about at home?
<i>- During the call...</i>

254
00:15:26,871 --> 00:15:29,474
- Hello?
<i>- ...Korea scored its first goal,</i>

255
00:15:30,942 --> 00:15:32,744
<i>and he was sniped and killed right after.</i>

256
00:15:33,344 --> 00:15:35,680
<i>The time was 11:02 p.m.</i>

257
00:15:40,752 --> 00:15:44,088
<i>The time it would take to walk quickly</i>
<i>from the rooftop to the fifth floor...</i>

258
00:15:44,722 --> 00:15:45,723
<i>is just over one minute.</i>

259
00:15:46,791 --> 00:15:49,961
<i>If she had found the collapsed Tae Sung</i>
<i>here at that time.</i>

260
00:15:53,364 --> 00:15:54,599
According to the record,

261
00:15:54,599 --> 00:15:56,901
the call was received
by the 911 dispatch center...

262
00:15:56,935 --> 00:16:00,405
at 11:07 p.m.
I know it was a long time ago,

263
00:16:00,438 --> 00:16:02,473
but do you happen
to remember the caller's voice?

264
00:16:02,473 --> 00:16:04,442
Anything like their tone or accent.

265
00:16:04,442 --> 00:16:07,045
It was a long time ago...

266
00:16:07,078 --> 00:16:09,314
I just remember
she sounded like a young woman.

267
00:16:10,148 --> 00:16:13,251
She kept it brief and hung up right away.

268
00:16:14,419 --> 00:16:17,889
I remember someone screaming
right before the call.

269
00:16:18,523 --> 00:16:21,392
I think that was when Korea scored
and won the game.

270
00:16:21,392 --> 00:16:25,230
<i>The time Korea scored</i>
<i>its second goal, 11:06 p.m.</i>

271
00:16:26,064 --> 00:16:28,366
<i>Right after that, the 911 call came in.</i>

272
00:16:36,407 --> 00:16:39,611
(Global IP Seminar)

273
00:16:41,412 --> 00:16:42,480
(Gate 3)

274
00:16:42,981 --> 00:16:44,716
<i>If we open the first-floor restrooms,</i>

275
00:16:44,749 --> 00:16:46,918
they get unbelievably dirty.

276
00:16:46,951 --> 00:16:50,321
<i>So the owner told me</i>
<i>to lock up all the doors...</i>

277
00:16:50,321 --> 00:16:51,689
<i>and not let anyone in.</i>

278
00:16:52,123 --> 00:16:55,093
But some crazy bastard
opened one of the doors...

279
00:16:55,093 --> 00:16:57,495
on the first floor without my knowledge.

280
00:16:59,864 --> 00:17:01,165
(Global IP Seminar)

281
00:17:10,275 --> 00:17:13,545
<i>Roughly 2 minutes to get</i>
<i>outside from the 5th-floor staircase.</i>

282
00:17:14,412 --> 00:17:15,680
<i>And right here,</i>

283
00:17:16,314 --> 00:17:19,784
<i>the pickpocket saw a woman.</i>

284
00:17:19,784 --> 00:17:21,186
<i>It was a woman?</i>

285
00:17:22,420 --> 00:17:24,189
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I'm sure.

286
00:17:25,190 --> 00:17:27,425
You think I can't tell a man from a woman?

287
00:17:28,226 --> 00:17:30,562
<i>It was my first time ever hitting someone,</i>

288
00:17:31,062 --> 00:17:32,397
<i>so I was worried about</i>
<i>what happened to him.</i>

289
00:17:32,931 --> 00:17:35,500
<i>I was hiding nearby</i>
<i>to see what was going on.</i>

290
00:17:36,534 --> 00:17:39,003
<i>Then a woman came out of the building.</i>

291
00:17:39,704 --> 00:17:41,272
<i>It was too dark to see her face,</i>

292
00:17:41,839 --> 00:17:43,708
<i>so I only saw her from behind</i>
<i>as she walked away.</i>

293
00:17:43,708 --> 00:17:44,976
<i>A red T-shirt...</i>

294
00:17:45,810 --> 00:17:47,212
The spiky headband? Yes.

295
00:17:47,245 --> 00:17:49,380
I saw that and thought,

296
00:17:49,981 --> 00:17:51,783
"Maybe one of the Red Devils
just used the restroom."

297
00:17:52,250 --> 00:17:53,318
That's what I thought.

298
00:17:53,785 --> 00:17:54,919
Red Devils?

299
00:17:57,088 --> 00:17:59,490
- Was she alone?
- Yes, alone.

300
00:17:59,858 --> 00:18:02,994
Do you remember anything else,
like her build or hairstyle?

301
00:18:03,761 --> 00:18:05,063
She was pretty tall.

302
00:18:05,496 --> 00:18:08,066
And she seemed slender.

303
00:18:09,767 --> 00:18:13,471
- I think her hair was short.
- Short hair...

304
00:18:13,872 --> 00:18:17,242
- Or was it tied up?
- Was she carrying or holding anything?

305
00:18:17,742 --> 00:18:18,910
Oh, right.

306
00:18:18,910 --> 00:18:22,013
She was carrying a big bag
on her shoulder.

307
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:23,681
About...

308
00:18:24,582 --> 00:18:25,583
About this big?

309
00:18:27,252 --> 00:18:28,419
A big bag on her shoulder?

310
00:18:28,453 --> 00:18:29,487
What time did you see her?

311
00:18:29,521 --> 00:18:32,323
Come on, how am I supposed to know that?

312
00:18:32,357 --> 00:18:34,225
But when she came out...

313
00:18:34,659 --> 00:18:39,364
I think Korea had just scored a goal.
Everyone was cheering like crazy.

314
00:18:40,265 --> 00:18:41,566
<i>It was nuts back then.</i>

315
00:18:42,100 --> 00:18:44,602
<i>Estimated to be around 11:10 p.m.</i>

316
00:18:45,403 --> 00:18:47,338
<i>Considering her movements and the time,</i>

317
00:18:48,039 --> 00:18:51,709
<i>the woman who reported Tae Sung</i>
<i>and the woman the pickpocket saw...</i>

318
00:18:51,709 --> 00:18:53,144
<i>are very likely the same person.</i>

319
00:18:54,746 --> 00:18:55,747
<i>In that case...</i>

320
00:18:56,614 --> 00:18:58,082
<i>Kingfisher is...</i>

321
00:18:58,449 --> 00:19:00,184
tall...

322
00:19:00,952 --> 00:19:03,922
and a well-built young man.

323
00:19:13,598 --> 00:19:14,699
(Horaengsseu)

324
00:19:15,667 --> 00:19:16,734
(Horaengsseu)

325
00:19:22,407 --> 00:19:23,641
<i>Why aren't you answering my calls again?</i>

326
00:19:26,978 --> 00:19:28,012
<i>Busy.</i>

327
00:19:29,314 --> 00:19:30,882
<i>Call me when you get a chance.</i>

328
00:19:31,616 --> 00:19:33,351
<i>I'll be waiting.</i>

329
00:19:33,351 --> 00:19:35,954
(Call me when you get a chance.
I'll be waiting.)

330
00:19:35,954 --> 00:19:37,021
(Why aren't you answering my calls again?)

331
00:19:37,021 --> 00:19:38,156
(Let's eat. What are you doing now?)

332
00:19:38,156 --> 00:19:39,257
(What are you doing this weekend?)

333
00:19:43,127 --> 00:19:45,830
I've only ever come here
to deliver chicken.

334
00:19:45,830 --> 00:19:47,699
It's my first time coming
for something like this.

335
00:19:48,299 --> 00:19:52,437
And I even ended up catching a criminal.
It's a really strange feeling.

336
00:19:53,238 --> 00:19:54,372
Chicken delivery?

337
00:19:54,372 --> 00:19:58,343
Sung Hoon always orders chicken
from our shop.

338
00:19:58,877 --> 00:20:01,913
Even though I tell him to just order
from somewhere closer,

339
00:20:01,913 --> 00:20:04,849
he says there are no chicken places
around here or something.

340
00:20:05,516 --> 00:20:08,353
How do you two know each other?

341
00:20:10,021 --> 00:20:11,856
From our judo class in elementary school.

342
00:20:11,856 --> 00:20:14,526
On his first day, he underestimated me
and picked a fight.

343
00:20:14,526 --> 00:20:16,361
But I took him down with a single throw.

344
00:20:16,394 --> 00:20:19,297
He must have been embarrassed
because he asked me to keep it a secret.

345
00:20:19,297 --> 00:20:21,399
So I suggested we be friends instead.

346
00:20:21,399 --> 00:20:23,434
Actually, he's two years older than me.

347
00:20:25,904 --> 00:20:26,905
Se Ah.

348
00:20:31,442 --> 00:20:32,644
Should we see each other again?

349
00:20:33,011 --> 00:20:34,012
Oh, you surprised me.

350
00:20:34,612 --> 00:20:36,548
Why?

351
00:20:38,149 --> 00:20:41,019
Because I'd like
to get to know you better.

352
00:20:41,619 --> 00:20:42,620
Really?

353
00:20:43,721 --> 00:20:45,456
Yes. Okay, let's meet up.

354
00:20:46,691 --> 00:20:49,027
Next time, let's make it
just the two of us.

355
00:20:51,196 --> 00:20:52,864
Because I think your friend likes you.

356
00:20:54,999 --> 00:20:56,000
What?

357
00:21:01,105 --> 00:21:03,107
Oh, no way.

358
00:21:03,107 --> 00:21:05,910
We've been through so much together.

359
00:21:07,212 --> 00:21:10,949
No, that's not it.

360
00:21:15,353 --> 00:21:18,323
- I'm home from school.
- You're back?

361
00:21:21,226 --> 00:21:22,861
Why is Mom in such a good mood?

362
00:21:23,361 --> 00:21:24,529
Oh, what a great day.

363
00:21:24,529 --> 00:21:27,098
Her five-year savings plan matures today.

364
00:21:27,131 --> 00:21:29,100
Wow, that's today?

365
00:21:29,133 --> 00:21:31,736
No wonder she's so happy,
getting a big lump sum.

366
00:21:32,637 --> 00:21:33,938
So, is she paying off a loan?

367
00:21:33,972 --> 00:21:36,774
She said she's renovating the kitchen.
The deep fryer is getting old.

368
00:21:37,742 --> 00:21:40,278
Hey, is this the last delivery?

369
00:21:40,278 --> 00:21:41,579
Yes, that's the last one.

370
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:45,149
You guys handle the deliveries.
Oh, what time is it?

371
00:21:45,516 --> 00:21:48,086
Oh, my. I'm going to stop by the bank,

372
00:21:48,119 --> 00:21:49,921
then go to the market
and head straight home.

373
00:21:50,321 --> 00:21:53,625
You all can come home later.
Let's close up early today.

374
00:21:54,259 --> 00:21:57,228
- Gosh.
- Are we having something special today?

375
00:21:57,262 --> 00:21:58,463
In that case, I want beef.

376
00:21:58,463 --> 00:21:59,831
Beef?

377
00:22:01,165 --> 00:22:03,368
- All right, let's.
- Yes!

378
00:22:03,368 --> 00:22:04,369
Oh, gosh.

379
00:22:04,402 --> 00:22:06,471
And tell Tae Sung's family to come over
if they have time.

380
00:22:08,873 --> 00:22:10,141
Mom, buy lots of meat.

381
00:22:10,174 --> 00:22:11,609
- Okay.
- Get the good stuff.

382
00:22:11,643 --> 00:22:13,177
- Bye, Mom.
- Okay, I'm off.

383
00:22:15,313 --> 00:22:17,181
I guess she's trying
to apologize with beef.

384
00:22:18,883 --> 00:22:20,385
Hey, you take that one.

385
00:22:20,418 --> 00:22:21,753
Pink Apartment.

386
00:22:21,786 --> 00:22:24,489
Gosh, you should've just called
a delivery service.

387
00:22:25,356 --> 00:22:28,960
- Hey, Sung Hoon stopped by yesterday.
- What? Why?

388
00:22:28,993 --> 00:22:30,428
What do you mean, why?
He came for chicken.

389
00:22:30,461 --> 00:22:33,331
He said he hasn't been able to reach you,
and he asked if something was wrong.

390
00:22:33,364 --> 00:22:34,799
Did you two have a fight?

391
00:22:34,832 --> 00:22:36,668
Come on, we're not kids.

392
00:22:37,669 --> 00:22:39,537
Where was it? Pink Apartment?

393
00:22:39,537 --> 00:22:40,605
I'm off.

394
00:22:40,605 --> 00:22:42,273
Hey, you need the building
and apartment number.

395
00:22:42,273 --> 00:22:43,942
Building 108, Apartment 504.

396
00:22:51,015 --> 00:22:52,016
Oh.

397
00:22:52,717 --> 00:22:53,751
Hello?

398
00:22:53,751 --> 00:22:55,987
Hello,
am I speaking with Ok Seon Ja?

399
00:22:55,987 --> 00:22:57,388
Yes, this is she.

400
00:22:57,388 --> 00:22:59,524
My name is Kim Mi So,
a manager at the government's...

401
00:22:59,524 --> 00:23:01,659
Financial Support Center.

402
00:23:01,693 --> 00:23:04,295
I'm calling because you've been selected
as a candidate...

403
00:23:04,329 --> 00:23:07,265
- for our new low-interest loan program.
- I have?

404
00:23:07,765 --> 00:23:09,100
Oh, why is that?

405
00:23:09,100 --> 00:23:10,835
But I don't need a loan.

406
00:23:10,869 --> 00:23:12,470
This targets
self-employed people...

407
00:23:12,470 --> 00:23:15,707
and offers a rate of 0.8 percent.

408
00:23:17,008 --> 00:23:18,943
Did you say 0.8 percent?

409
00:23:18,943 --> 00:23:20,812
Yes. I looked up your records,

410
00:23:20,812 --> 00:23:24,515
and it shows you have
an existing loan from Hanup Bank.

411
00:23:24,515 --> 00:23:27,652
Oh, yes. I do.

412
00:23:27,685 --> 00:23:29,220
Was that at 4.2 percent?

413
00:23:29,754 --> 00:23:31,589
Our rate is much lower,

414
00:23:31,589 --> 00:23:33,958
so a lot of people switch over
to save on interest.

415
00:23:34,392 --> 00:23:36,995
Some people have even saved
1,000 dollars a month.

416
00:23:36,995 --> 00:23:38,296
Thousand dollars?

417
00:23:38,329 --> 00:23:39,631
Yes, a 1,000 dollars.

418
00:23:40,798 --> 00:23:42,066
Oh, my goodness.

419
00:23:42,567 --> 00:23:45,837
- Wow, that must be nice.
- However, there is one condition.

420
00:23:45,837 --> 00:23:49,440
In order to use our loan,
you must first pay off your existing one.

421
00:23:50,208 --> 00:23:52,977
What do you think?
Are you interested?

422
00:23:52,977 --> 00:23:54,779
Oh, well, it's just that...

423
00:23:55,680 --> 00:23:57,916
I should ask my kids first.

424
00:23:57,916 --> 00:24:00,451
But the offer is only valid for today.

425
00:24:00,451 --> 00:24:02,220
If you're not interested,
I have to contact...

426
00:24:02,220 --> 00:24:03,521
the next person on the list.

427
00:24:03,555 --> 00:24:06,057
No, wait, just a moment.

428
00:24:09,194 --> 00:24:11,596
I'll do it. What do I need to do?

429
00:24:12,130 --> 00:24:15,366
You'll have to pay off the loan
by today. Will that be possible?

430
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,734
What?

431
00:24:17,702 --> 00:24:21,039
Well, I happen to have the money.

432
00:24:22,040 --> 00:24:24,442
But the banks are closed now.

433
00:24:24,442 --> 00:24:26,411
In that case, I'll connect you with...

434
00:24:26,411 --> 00:24:28,279
a Hanup Bank branch
that's affiliated with us.

435
00:24:32,083 --> 00:24:33,151
(Are you requested to transfer money
from Financial Supervisory Office?)

436
00:24:45,163 --> 00:24:49,133
(Upgrade Your Daily Life With One Choice,
Hanup Bank)

437
00:24:50,902 --> 00:24:51,903
Let's go.

438
00:24:52,670 --> 00:24:56,507
Honey, did you hear?
Your mom wants to have a steak dinner.

439
00:24:56,507 --> 00:24:57,575
When are you finishing up?

440
00:24:57,575 --> 00:24:59,510
I'm on assignment,
but I don't think it'll take long.

441
00:24:59,510 --> 00:25:01,980
- I'll head over as soon as I'm done.
- Okay, got it.

442
00:25:18,162 --> 00:25:19,163
(Ok's Flower Shop)

443
00:25:19,163 --> 00:25:20,732
- I'll get going then.
- Thank you.

444
00:25:20,732 --> 00:25:21,733
Okay.

445
00:25:34,946 --> 00:25:36,514
(Ok's Flower Shop)

446
00:25:38,182 --> 00:25:40,084
(Ok's Flower Shop)

447
00:25:40,485 --> 00:25:42,053
I didn't know this was in my neighborhood.

448
00:25:43,221 --> 00:25:45,156
- Welcome.
- Hello.

449
00:25:48,259 --> 00:25:50,862
I never knew there was such a beautiful
flower shop in my neighborhood.

450
00:25:50,895 --> 00:25:53,665
Oh, so you live around here.

451
00:25:54,299 --> 00:25:57,101
Well, people who usually drive
might not have noticed it.

452
00:25:57,535 --> 00:26:00,672
Right. I guess most men
aren't that interested in flowers.

453
00:26:01,272 --> 00:26:04,209
I imagine your main customers
are women from the neighborhood.

454
00:26:04,209 --> 00:26:05,210
Why do you say that?

455
00:26:05,210 --> 00:26:09,280
Plenty of men come in to buy flowers
for their wives or girlfriends.

456
00:26:10,548 --> 00:26:11,583
I see.

457
00:26:11,983 --> 00:26:13,451
- I'll just...
- Yes?

458
00:26:13,484 --> 00:26:14,485
Yes.

459
00:26:23,795 --> 00:26:26,264
Are you looking for any particular flower?

460
00:26:28,333 --> 00:26:29,534
What's the meaning of this flower?

461
00:26:30,802 --> 00:26:32,070
The sunflower?

462
00:26:32,070 --> 00:26:35,073
It symbolizes hope, positivity,
and encouragement.

463
00:26:35,073 --> 00:26:37,375
They're popular
for celebrations, hospital visits,

464
00:26:37,375 --> 00:26:39,410
or as a gift
when you're visiting someone's home.

465
00:26:39,410 --> 00:26:41,512
They're also said to cleanse a home
of dark energy...

466
00:26:41,546 --> 00:26:44,349
and fill it with bright, positive energy.

467
00:26:44,816 --> 00:26:46,184
I see. So that's what it means.

468
00:26:52,524 --> 00:26:56,427
Actually, I came here
to ask you something.

469
00:26:57,395 --> 00:26:59,030
(Kwon Tae Sung, Reporter of
Investigative Reporting Team, Not Today)

470
00:26:59,731 --> 00:27:01,165
I was hoping you could tell me
about the person...

471
00:27:01,199 --> 00:27:03,535
who sends flowers to a boy
named Yeon Cheol.

472
00:27:04,369 --> 00:27:05,403
Yeon Cheol...

473
00:27:06,504 --> 00:27:08,940
The boy from the welfare center.

474
00:27:08,940 --> 00:27:09,941
Right.

475
00:27:09,941 --> 00:27:12,377
I just take the order
and have them sent out.

476
00:27:15,079 --> 00:27:16,981
What about the meanings of the flowers?

477
00:27:16,981 --> 00:27:20,018
I heard a card explaining the meaning
of them is sent every time.

478
00:27:20,018 --> 00:27:21,319
Oh, I'm the one who does that.

479
00:27:21,319 --> 00:27:23,755
There's never a message
included with the order,

480
00:27:23,755 --> 00:27:25,557
and it feels a little empty
to send them without one.

481
00:27:27,525 --> 00:27:30,728
But an employee there
remembered the message on the first card.

482
00:27:30,728 --> 00:27:31,763
So does that mean you also?

483
00:27:31,796 --> 00:27:33,164
The first card...

484
00:27:33,765 --> 00:27:35,366
Well... I suppose I must have.

485
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:37,402
Do you remember what you wrote,
by any chance?

486
00:27:37,936 --> 00:27:40,238
I'm not sure. What was it?

487
00:27:41,773 --> 00:27:44,943
<i>"I hope you find</i>
<i>your own beautiful scenery."</i>

488
00:27:44,943 --> 00:27:46,411
<i>That was the one line written on it.</i>

489
00:27:46,844 --> 00:27:49,314
Something about hoping
he'd always smile brightly like a flower.

490
00:27:50,481 --> 00:27:52,951
Oh, that's right. I did.

491
00:27:52,984 --> 00:27:54,986
I suppose since it was for a child.

492
00:27:55,954 --> 00:27:58,323
Right.

493
00:28:02,827 --> 00:28:04,462
Hello.

494
00:28:06,564 --> 00:28:08,900
Hello, I'm from the Gwanghwamun branch
of Hanup Bank.

495
00:28:08,900 --> 00:28:10,468
My name is Gwon Dong Heon.

496
00:28:11,102 --> 00:28:12,237
(Gwon Dong Heon)

497
00:28:12,904 --> 00:28:16,674
How do I know this is real
just from a business card?

498
00:28:17,208 --> 00:28:19,944
It's just,
you can't be too careful these days.

499
00:28:19,944 --> 00:28:21,913
Yes, of course. I understand.

500
00:28:21,913 --> 00:28:26,351
Here, this is my bank ID card.

501
00:28:26,384 --> 00:28:27,785
- Okay.
- Yes, and...

502
00:28:28,186 --> 00:28:31,589
- These are the loan repayment documents.
- Okay.

503
00:28:31,589 --> 00:28:32,957
Please take your time and read it over,

504
00:28:32,991 --> 00:28:34,192
and then you can sign.

505
00:28:36,594 --> 00:28:40,765
That's right, it is. Yes.
Hold on, just a moment.

506
00:28:40,765 --> 00:28:42,233
- Okay.
- Yes.

507
00:28:42,233 --> 00:28:43,234
Yes, please take your time.

508
00:28:50,875 --> 00:28:54,279
- I've signed it.
- Yes, okay.

509
00:28:54,279 --> 00:28:55,413
But...

510
00:28:57,048 --> 00:28:59,951
This will take care of the loan payment,
right?

511
00:28:59,984 --> 00:29:03,788
Of course.
You called the bank yourself, ma'am.

512
00:29:03,821 --> 00:29:05,857
- Well...
- All right, then.

513
00:29:06,925 --> 00:29:07,926
Wait.

514
00:29:09,327 --> 00:29:10,328
I mean...

515
00:29:11,629 --> 00:29:12,630
Ma'am.

516
00:29:13,898 --> 00:29:17,635
Our Team Leader is waiting
and can't leave work.

517
00:29:18,269 --> 00:29:22,240
Oh, my goodness. I feel so bad.
I feel terrible.

518
00:29:23,374 --> 00:29:26,311
Oh, I'm so sorry. You're busy,
and I'm keeping you from going home,

519
00:29:26,311 --> 00:29:28,680
and you even came all this way. Thank you.

520
00:29:28,713 --> 00:29:30,949
Not at all.
We're the ones who are grateful.

521
00:29:30,949 --> 00:29:32,317
Your precious money.

522
00:29:32,750 --> 00:29:35,186
- Yes.
- I'll make sure it's delivered safely.

523
00:29:35,220 --> 00:29:36,955
- Okay.
- Yes.

524
00:29:36,955 --> 00:29:39,157
Please, make sure
you take good care of it.

525
00:29:39,190 --> 00:29:40,692
Yes. Go on inside.

526
00:29:40,692 --> 00:29:42,660
- Okay, yes, goodbye.
- Don't you worry.

527
00:29:42,660 --> 00:29:44,128
Yes, be careful with the money.

528
00:29:44,128 --> 00:29:45,897
- Please, go on inside.
- Okay.

529
00:29:45,897 --> 00:29:47,632
- Call us again anytime.
- Okay.

530
00:29:50,869 --> 00:29:52,937
- Yes.
- Oh, my.

531
00:29:57,242 --> 00:29:58,409
(Boss)

532
00:29:59,510 --> 00:30:02,380
Darn. That old lady, she's so suspicious.

533
00:30:02,380 --> 00:30:04,449
Does she think it makes her look smart?
Darn it.

534
00:30:05,049 --> 00:30:06,451
Of course. I got it.

535
00:30:07,418 --> 00:30:09,454
But the incentive is ten percent, right?

536
00:30:11,856 --> 00:30:13,691
Yes, I'll meet you there.

537
00:30:16,461 --> 00:30:17,795
Let's go.

538
00:30:19,264 --> 00:30:20,632
Hello.

539
00:30:21,165 --> 00:30:22,901
Oh, hi.

540
00:30:24,602 --> 00:30:27,605
- Excuse me, can we get out?
- Oh, yes. Sorry about that.

541
00:30:27,605 --> 00:30:28,606
Thank you.

542
00:30:32,076 --> 00:30:33,077
Goodbye.

543
00:30:35,213 --> 00:30:37,582
- Let's go.
- Gosh.

544
00:30:38,383 --> 00:30:39,951
Why did I just get a chill down my spine?

545
00:30:40,919 --> 00:30:43,221
What? Is there a problem?

546
00:30:43,221 --> 00:30:44,822
Grandma!

547
00:30:44,856 --> 00:30:46,591
Oh, my sweet little girl.
You're here?

548
00:30:47,392 --> 00:30:49,327
Mom, did someone stop by?

549
00:30:49,961 --> 00:30:51,229
Someone from the bank.

550
00:30:51,262 --> 00:30:53,164
He was such a hard-working young man.

551
00:30:53,198 --> 00:30:55,767
He came all the way to a customer's house
after hours.

552
00:30:55,767 --> 00:30:57,602
- Someone from the bank?
- Yes.

553
00:30:58,870 --> 00:31:00,505
Mom, did you give him any money?

554
00:31:00,538 --> 00:31:02,040
Yes, of course.

555
00:31:02,040 --> 00:31:03,975
He said he was here
to collect the loan payment.

556
00:31:03,975 --> 00:31:05,243
The money I got from my savings today...

557
00:31:06,878 --> 00:31:09,714
What? What's wrong?

558
00:31:09,714 --> 00:31:11,950
I think that was a Voice Phishing scam.

559
00:31:11,950 --> 00:31:13,117
Stay here with Yul.

560
00:31:14,652 --> 00:31:15,653
Oh, my.

561
00:31:17,455 --> 00:31:22,093
Oh, my goodness.
Oh, what do I do? Oh, my.

562
00:31:39,544 --> 00:31:43,281
Oh, that man. Why would he do that?
Oh, no. What is she going to do?

563
00:31:43,314 --> 00:31:44,315
What the hell?

564
00:31:44,983 --> 00:31:47,952
It's that woman from before. Darn it.

565
00:31:49,487 --> 00:31:51,623
- Get out.
- What the hell?

566
00:31:52,390 --> 00:31:53,391
Am I caught?

567
00:31:53,424 --> 00:31:55,226
Darn it.

568
00:32:04,569 --> 00:32:07,472
Darn it, is that son of a gun crazy?

569
00:32:08,439 --> 00:32:09,474
So you want to play, right?

570
00:32:21,419 --> 00:32:22,420
Oh, my goodness.

571
00:32:24,756 --> 00:32:27,759
Oh, my. Oh, dear.

572
00:32:31,496 --> 00:32:35,033
Oh, dear Lord. But wait,
what did I just see?

573
00:32:35,033 --> 00:32:37,035
- Yes, ma'am.
- I need you to run a plate number.

574
00:32:38,303 --> 00:32:40,572
- Se Ah.
- Bo Na, where are you going?

575
00:32:40,572 --> 00:32:42,340
I have to catch that car.
It's Voice Phishing.

576
00:32:42,373 --> 00:32:44,909
- What? Voice Phishing?
- Yes.

577
00:32:44,943 --> 00:32:47,278
- That... That car?
- Yes.

578
00:32:47,312 --> 00:32:48,613
Assistant Manager Ki,
I'll take care of it.

579
00:32:48,646 --> 00:32:49,914
Ma'am...

580
00:32:56,921 --> 00:32:58,189
Voice Phishing?

581
00:33:00,291 --> 00:33:01,860
Oh, so does that mean those two women...

582
00:33:04,262 --> 00:33:05,530
Gosh.

583
00:33:07,265 --> 00:33:09,000
Of all the people he could have scammed...

584
00:33:11,536 --> 00:33:14,572
Hey, but Bo Na,
why are we chasing that car?

585
00:33:14,606 --> 00:33:16,374
Who is the victim?

586
00:33:16,374 --> 00:33:17,775
Our mother.

587
00:33:17,775 --> 00:33:21,079
- He took her savings and ran.
- What? That psycho.

588
00:33:21,379 --> 00:33:22,547
Bo Na, hold on tight.

589
00:33:39,931 --> 00:33:42,133
- Se Ah, pull over.
- What? Why?

590
00:33:42,667 --> 00:33:43,668
Hurry.

591
00:33:44,636 --> 00:33:46,271
Wait, Bo Na, what are you going to do?

592
00:33:48,206 --> 00:33:51,509
- What?
- I have to get Mother's money. I'm off.

593
00:33:51,509 --> 00:33:52,644
Bo Na, you can't go alone...

594
00:33:53,444 --> 00:33:54,846
Bo Na, you have to be careful.

595
00:33:56,314 --> 00:33:58,082
I am going to get you.

596
00:34:26,344 --> 00:34:27,679
Darn it.

597
00:34:28,146 --> 00:34:29,948
Man, I have been doing
a lot of running lately.

598
00:34:43,428 --> 00:34:44,495
What is her problem?

599
00:35:02,614 --> 00:35:04,515
- Are you all right?
- Are you all right, sir?

600
00:35:36,981 --> 00:35:38,182
Gosh. What the hell.

601
00:35:39,117 --> 00:35:41,052
Darn it.

602
00:35:53,498 --> 00:35:55,700
Hey, what gives? Are you a cop?

603
00:35:56,034 --> 00:35:59,003
- I'm scarier than the cops.
- Darn it.

604
00:35:59,470 --> 00:36:03,775
A lady who is not even a cop.
You have got a serious death wish.

605
00:36:05,076 --> 00:36:08,746
Oh, what a shame. There is no one around
and no CCTV cameras either.

606
00:36:09,614 --> 00:36:10,615
Is that right?

607
00:36:11,683 --> 00:36:13,251
Perfect. Get up.

608
00:36:13,251 --> 00:36:14,786
What? Darn it.

609
00:36:16,454 --> 00:36:17,956
(Southern Seoul Police Station)

610
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:23,795
We can get my mother-in-law's money back
right away, correct?

611
00:36:23,828 --> 00:36:25,897
- My mother-in-law collapsed and...
- Bo Na.

612
00:36:25,897 --> 00:36:28,132
- Kwon Se Ah.
- Dong Jin.

613
00:36:28,166 --> 00:36:30,768
- Oh, hello.
- Bo Na, are you okay?

614
00:36:31,369 --> 00:36:32,570
Yes, I am fine.

615
00:36:32,604 --> 00:36:34,606
You are so busy.
You did not have to come all this way.

616
00:36:34,606 --> 00:36:35,940
Why did you chase them?
That was dangerous.

617
00:36:35,940 --> 00:36:37,208
You are not hurt anywhere, are you?

618
00:36:37,208 --> 00:36:40,511
I am not hurt.
Well, thank you for your concern.

619
00:36:40,545 --> 00:36:41,646
- Oh, Inspector Lee.
- I am sorry.

620
00:36:41,679 --> 00:36:42,747
Do you know them?

621
00:36:42,747 --> 00:36:44,582
Yes, they're family.

622
00:36:44,616 --> 00:36:46,684
Sorry? Family?

623
00:36:47,318 --> 00:36:48,653
Yes. Where are those
Voice Phishing bastards?

624
00:36:48,686 --> 00:36:49,921
Oh, yes. Over there.

625
00:36:52,223 --> 00:36:53,591
What's with the state of those bastards?

626
00:36:53,625 --> 00:36:55,460
Well, they tried to get away
when these two chased them,

627
00:36:55,493 --> 00:36:57,161
so I guess they fell and rolled around.

628
00:36:58,196 --> 00:36:59,931
No, that is not what happened, sir.

629
00:36:59,931 --> 00:37:01,132
Listen,
that son of a gun in the red clothes...

630
00:37:01,132 --> 00:37:03,368
judo-flipped me. Three times.

631
00:37:03,401 --> 00:37:06,638
That lady hit me here with a coke,

632
00:37:06,638 --> 00:37:09,040
kicked me here, and kneed me
right here. Look.

633
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:10,041
A knee kick? Seriously?

634
00:37:10,041 --> 00:37:12,744
Honestly, they were
the ones making a scene.

635
00:37:13,444 --> 00:37:15,013
Unbelievable. It's ridiculous, right?

636
00:37:15,046 --> 00:37:18,783
When can we expect to get
my mother-in-law's money back?

637
00:37:18,783 --> 00:37:19,984
Well, it has to go through
the proper channels,

638
00:37:19,984 --> 00:37:21,252
so it will take some time.

639
00:37:21,252 --> 00:37:22,487
But we caught them running away...

640
00:37:22,487 --> 00:37:25,490
Looks like these punks still don't get it.
They're just spouting nonsense.

641
00:37:25,523 --> 00:37:28,059
I guess so. Hey, you, get over here.
What was that? "That son of a gun?"

642
00:37:28,059 --> 00:37:29,661
Who are you calling "a son of gun,"
you punk?

643
00:37:29,661 --> 00:37:31,129
Hey, get that mouth over here.

644
00:37:31,596 --> 00:37:33,731
- You're dead if I come in there.
- He's so cool.

645
00:37:34,566 --> 00:37:36,701
- Honey.
- Hey, dear.

646
00:37:36,734 --> 00:37:38,336
- Mother.
- Mom. Tae Sung.

647
00:37:38,369 --> 00:37:40,672
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

648
00:37:40,672 --> 00:37:43,274
I'm perfectly fine. Don't worry, honey.

649
00:37:43,274 --> 00:37:46,010
- Are you sure you're okay?
- Yes, I'm fine. Really.

650
00:37:46,477 --> 00:37:47,579
Gosh, seriously...

651
00:37:48,413 --> 00:37:51,449
Oh, my money.
Officer, what about my money?

652
00:37:51,449 --> 00:37:53,885
We'll return it to you
after it goes through our procedures.

653
00:37:53,885 --> 00:37:55,286
Please don't worry.

654
00:37:55,820 --> 00:37:56,888
What a relief.

655
00:37:57,689 --> 00:37:59,824
- That money is so important...
- Are you really okay?

656
00:38:00,625 --> 00:38:03,294
Usually, it's hard to get the money back
in these cases.

657
00:38:03,294 --> 00:38:05,296
These two did something amazing.

658
00:38:06,231 --> 00:38:07,899
- Why are you...
- Why would you chase after them?

659
00:38:07,966 --> 00:38:11,836
You should have called the police.
Do you have any idea how worried I was?

660
00:38:11,836 --> 00:38:14,105
- I had no choice because...
- Excuse me, brother.

661
00:38:14,105 --> 00:38:16,341
I guess you can't see
your only sister over here.

662
00:38:16,875 --> 00:38:18,643
Of course you're fine.

663
00:38:18,643 --> 00:38:20,078
- Oh, what was that?
- What?

664
00:38:20,111 --> 00:38:22,614
Come on, at least pretend to be worried.

665
00:38:22,614 --> 00:38:24,349
I have no doubt whatsoever
that you are perfectly fine.

666
00:38:24,349 --> 00:38:26,351
Oh, seriously, don't be like that.

667
00:38:27,018 --> 00:38:28,386
Be careful.

668
00:38:29,153 --> 00:38:30,922
It's my money. Why does getting it back

669
00:38:30,922 --> 00:38:33,291
- have to be so complicated?
- I know, right?

670
00:38:33,291 --> 00:38:35,593
Wow, I can't believe I'm here again.

671
00:38:35,994 --> 00:38:39,397
Caught criminals again. Fulfilling day.

672
00:38:39,397 --> 00:38:41,032
Oh, honestly.

673
00:38:41,466 --> 00:38:45,703
Still, even so,
did you really have to go that far?

674
00:38:46,771 --> 00:38:49,140
Oh, of course.

675
00:38:49,140 --> 00:38:51,442
Mother, you worked so hard
from dawn until dusk,

676
00:38:51,442 --> 00:38:53,144
saving every last penny
of that precious money.

677
00:38:53,578 --> 00:38:55,480
We had to get it back.

678
00:38:56,548 --> 00:39:00,251
Anyway, it would have been a disaster
if it hadn't been for you.

679
00:39:01,452 --> 00:39:02,487
Th...

680
00:39:04,022 --> 00:39:05,023
Th...

681
00:39:06,357 --> 00:39:07,458
Th...

682
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:11,229
Th... Let's go get some barbecue.

683
00:39:11,229 --> 00:39:14,065
Is it that hard to say, "Thank you?"

684
00:39:16,434 --> 00:39:17,769
Let's go.

685
00:39:18,236 --> 00:39:22,640
- Come on, Mother. Let's go together.
- Is it pride or stubbornness? Geez.

686
00:39:22,640 --> 00:39:23,641
Kwon Se Ah.

687
00:39:30,715 --> 00:39:32,250
You're just going to leave
without saying goodbye?

688
00:39:40,291 --> 00:39:41,659
Why are you avoiding me?

689
00:39:41,659 --> 00:39:44,429
What? When did I? I'm not avoiding you.

690
00:39:45,029 --> 00:39:46,431
Did I do something wrong?

691
00:39:46,431 --> 00:39:51,202
No, it's not that you did
something wrong...

692
00:39:52,237 --> 00:39:53,972
Why are you trailing off?
That's not like you.

693
00:39:54,372 --> 00:39:56,174
Just spit it out. What is it?

694
00:39:56,741 --> 00:39:58,576
Is it possible...

695
00:40:01,346 --> 00:40:04,382
Stop beating around the bush
and just tell me.

696
00:40:04,382 --> 00:40:05,617
What about me?

697
00:40:05,617 --> 00:40:07,018
Do you like me?

698
00:40:15,760 --> 00:40:18,830
Hey, so that's it. That's hilarious.

699
00:40:20,198 --> 00:40:24,002
Hey. It's not that funny.
Forget I said anything.

700
00:40:24,035 --> 00:40:28,106
I was just wondering,
so I asked. That's all.

701
00:40:28,106 --> 00:40:30,275
Oh, I can't believe this.

702
00:40:34,212 --> 00:40:36,080
So that's what it was.

703
00:40:36,114 --> 00:40:38,182
What? What, what, what was?

704
00:40:38,816 --> 00:40:42,020
So that's why I'd get so annoyed
when I couldn't reach you,

705
00:40:42,053 --> 00:40:43,555
and why I was curious about
what you were doing,

706
00:40:43,555 --> 00:40:46,624
and why I wanted to see your face
and hear your voice.

707
00:40:48,459 --> 00:40:49,561
What did you say?

708
00:40:50,562 --> 00:40:52,197
So it's true.

709
00:40:55,867 --> 00:40:57,235
I guess I do like you.

710
00:41:09,411 --> 00:41:10,945
I'll let you know
when the results are out.

711
00:41:10,956 --> 00:41:12,157
It'll take a few days.

712
00:41:14,657 --> 00:41:16,392
Thanks for coming. I know you're busy.

713
00:41:16,392 --> 00:41:17,494
Of course I came.

714
00:41:18,094 --> 00:41:19,863
It's about your wife.
You think I wouldn't?

715
00:41:21,831 --> 00:41:24,334
I guess married couples
start to become alike.

716
00:41:24,334 --> 00:41:27,137
I can't believe your wife
was fearless enough to chase after him.

717
00:41:28,204 --> 00:41:30,306
She doesn't take after me.
She's always had nerves of steel.

718
00:41:31,574 --> 00:41:34,077
Well, she's different from you,
who got blindsided.

719
00:41:35,278 --> 00:41:37,180
Hey, Bo Na was the one who hit him
in the back of the head,

720
00:41:37,180 --> 00:41:38,314
with a coke, no less.

721
00:41:39,983 --> 00:41:41,184
What?

722
00:41:41,184 --> 00:41:44,988
It's not you who needs to protect Bo Na.
It's Bo Na who needs to protect you.

723
00:41:47,190 --> 00:41:49,859
Hey, it's not like that. Come on.

724
00:41:53,663 --> 00:41:56,366
I had something to ask you. Perfect.

725
00:41:56,366 --> 00:41:58,868
- Something to ask me?
- Yes.

726
00:42:01,271 --> 00:42:05,175
The man you said you saw, Kingfisher.

727
00:42:07,444 --> 00:42:09,913
- Hey, about that, just wait until I...
- Hear me out.

728
00:42:12,282 --> 00:42:14,451
Is there any chance you were mistaken?

729
00:42:16,920 --> 00:42:20,123
Why would you assume I'm mistaken
before you've even heard me out?

730
00:42:20,123 --> 00:42:22,192
I ask a question,
and you answer with a question.

731
00:42:22,192 --> 00:42:23,593
Okay, next question.

732
00:42:23,593 --> 00:42:25,862
During the World Cup pickpocket incident
eight years ago,

733
00:42:26,596 --> 00:42:29,866
did you ever find the woman
who called 911 for you?

734
00:42:29,866 --> 00:42:32,268
No. If I couldn't find her back then,
how am I supposed to find her now?

735
00:42:32,735 --> 00:42:35,605
If I'd found her, I would've met her
long ago. She saved my life.

736
00:42:37,140 --> 00:42:38,441
But why are you suddenly asking about her?

737
00:42:38,441 --> 00:42:40,543
You should have the audio
on your phone, right?

738
00:42:40,543 --> 00:42:42,545
Reporters usually set their phones
to auto-record calls.

739
00:42:42,545 --> 00:42:43,780
You've never listened to it?

740
00:42:43,780 --> 00:42:46,549
Of course I did. Right after I woke up.

741
00:42:47,016 --> 00:42:48,485
But how would I know from her voice?

742
00:42:48,485 --> 00:42:51,521
Am I supposed to compare it
to the voice of every woman in Korea?

743
00:42:52,555 --> 00:42:54,991
Do you still have that phone?

744
00:42:55,859 --> 00:42:58,027
- My phone from back then?
- Yes.

745
00:42:59,763 --> 00:43:01,598
I got rid of it ages ago.
That was so long ago.

746
00:43:02,866 --> 00:43:04,701
Seriously, why are you
looking for that woman?

747
00:43:10,039 --> 00:43:15,044
Because she could have been a witness
to Kingfisher, or an accomplice.

748
00:43:16,613 --> 00:43:17,680
Or...

749
00:43:18,848 --> 00:43:20,216
She could be Kingfisher herself.

750
00:43:22,018 --> 00:43:23,019
What?

751
00:43:24,287 --> 00:43:25,321
Tae Sung.

752
00:43:26,523 --> 00:43:29,058
So stop with the stories.
Don't make things confusing.

753
00:43:29,726 --> 00:43:32,662
Otherwise, I'll send you
an official summons soon.

754
00:43:32,662 --> 00:43:35,098
You know I'm on
the Kingfisher task force, right?

755
00:43:47,777 --> 00:43:49,979
But this meat
is really good today.

756
00:43:50,313 --> 00:43:51,347
Where is it from?

757
00:43:51,381 --> 00:43:53,450
This is Sangju Beef. Sangju Beef.

758
00:43:53,817 --> 00:43:57,220
I asked for the very best they had,

759
00:43:57,220 --> 00:43:59,722
so everyone, eat your fill today.

760
00:43:59,722 --> 00:44:00,723
Okay.

761
00:44:02,959 --> 00:44:06,162
She couldn't wait to have beef,
so what's wrong with her?

762
00:44:07,263 --> 00:44:09,499
Leave her be.
She must be full from happiness.

763
00:44:12,335 --> 00:44:13,336
What's with him now?

764
00:44:13,837 --> 00:44:16,506
- Hey, the meat's going to burn.
- Oh, right.

765
00:44:18,908 --> 00:44:20,643
That one?

766
00:44:21,578 --> 00:44:22,779
Yul's mom...

767
00:44:23,179 --> 00:44:26,449
Goodness, having these here
really brightens up the house, doesn't it?

768
00:44:28,151 --> 00:44:31,387
I bought them at the flower shop
up the street on my way here, Mom.

769
00:44:32,489 --> 00:44:36,226
They say that sunflowers purify
a home's dark energy

770
00:44:36,259 --> 00:44:38,795
and fill it with bright, positive energy.

771
00:44:39,462 --> 00:44:40,997
I see.

772
00:44:40,997 --> 00:44:42,699
Oh, so that's what sunflowers do.

773
00:44:42,699 --> 00:44:45,668
By the way, Bo Na,
you're really something else.

774
00:44:45,702 --> 00:44:48,505
How did you even think
of chasing him down all by yourself?

775
00:44:49,939 --> 00:44:51,307
Well...

776
00:44:53,076 --> 00:44:57,547
I think my body just reacted on its own.

777
00:44:57,580 --> 00:45:00,250
- Se Ah was there, so I just...
- That was so cool.

778
00:45:02,852 --> 00:45:04,654
Mom, this meat is so delicious.

779
00:45:04,654 --> 00:45:06,055
Yes, it is.

780
00:45:06,656 --> 00:45:08,024
Help yourself.

781
00:45:08,024 --> 00:45:11,060
Yul, let's have another bite.
It's not hot, is it?

782
00:45:12,228 --> 00:45:13,863
Don't you ever do that again.

783
00:45:13,863 --> 00:45:15,565
You have to call the police first.
All right?

784
00:45:16,366 --> 00:45:18,468
He doesn't care
if his own mother gets scammed.

785
00:45:18,468 --> 00:45:20,370
All he worries about is his precious wife.

786
00:45:20,370 --> 00:45:21,871
Oh, here we go again.

787
00:45:21,905 --> 00:45:23,640
Mom, are you proud that you got scammed?

788
00:45:24,274 --> 00:45:25,742
How could you fall for that?

789
00:45:25,775 --> 00:45:27,076
Stop rubbing it in.

790
00:45:27,610 --> 00:45:29,579
You would've fallen for it too
if you had got that call.

791
00:45:29,579 --> 00:45:30,980
No, I wouldn't have.

792
00:45:30,980 --> 00:45:32,048
This is good.

793
00:45:32,482 --> 00:45:35,785
How desperate do you have to be
to steal someone's hard-earned money?

794
00:45:37,420 --> 00:45:39,789
You should eat rice too.

795
00:45:45,795 --> 00:45:47,363
Wow, this is really good.

796
00:45:48,965 --> 00:45:51,634
Hey, look at this.

797
00:45:51,634 --> 00:45:56,039
Do you know how hard it was
to get this meat?

798
00:46:12,155 --> 00:46:14,190
Honey. I'll do it.

799
00:46:14,190 --> 00:46:16,226
No, stop it. It'll only take me a second.

800
00:46:16,259 --> 00:46:18,061
- Don't.
- Kwon Tae Sung.

801
00:46:24,067 --> 00:46:25,068
Mom, it's not like that.

802
00:46:25,101 --> 00:46:28,004
Since the women did the prep,
I'll just do the dishes.

803
00:46:33,109 --> 00:46:35,411
It's greasy, so use hot water.

804
00:46:36,146 --> 00:46:37,814
Make sure you rinse them well.

805
00:46:47,490 --> 00:46:48,491
Here.

806
00:46:54,431 --> 00:46:56,099
Here, just pull it all up like this...

807
00:46:57,834 --> 00:46:58,968
All right.

808
00:47:09,879 --> 00:47:14,150
- You said...
- It's because...

809
00:47:14,150 --> 00:47:17,420
Oh, Mom. I told you it was impossible.

810
00:47:17,420 --> 00:47:18,688
Come on, it's nothing...

811
00:47:21,157 --> 00:47:22,959
(Ok's Flower Shop)

812
00:47:39,809 --> 00:47:43,713
(Interviews with Associates
of The Kingfisher Victim)

813
00:47:55,358 --> 00:47:57,393
<i>Seriously, why are you</i>
<i>looking for that woman?</i>

814
00:47:57,393 --> 00:48:01,297
Because she could have been a witness
to Kingfisher, or an accomplice.

815
00:48:02,866 --> 00:48:05,468
Or she could be Kingfisher herself.

816
00:48:26,890 --> 00:48:28,892
<i>Your husband</i>
<i>came by the shop today.</i>

817
00:48:29,692 --> 00:48:30,994
<i>It looks like he went to see Cheol.</i>

818
00:48:31,895 --> 00:48:33,763
<i>He was asking about the person</i>
<i>who sends the flowers.</i>

819
00:48:35,799 --> 00:48:39,402
<i>I gave him a vague answer,</i>
<i>but I thought you should know.</i>

820
00:48:51,314 --> 00:48:52,949
(Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency)

821
00:48:52,949 --> 00:48:55,418
It's clear that only one person
fired the gun.

822
00:48:55,819 --> 00:48:57,253
However, as you can see,

823
00:48:57,253 --> 00:48:58,455
we cannot rule out that
there was an accomplice involved

824
00:48:58,455 --> 00:48:59,489
for the rest of the process
except the shooting,

825
00:48:59,522 --> 00:49:02,992
and that there's also the possibility of
a separate team operating independently.

826
00:49:03,026 --> 00:49:04,527
(Kingfisher Special Investigation Team)

827
00:49:04,527 --> 00:49:07,831
So you're saying Kingfisher has
an organized network of accomplices?

828
00:49:09,966 --> 00:49:11,267
That makes sense.

829
00:49:11,267 --> 00:49:14,604
Yes. In that case, their M.O

830
00:49:14,604 --> 00:49:17,173
is likely not limited to sniping.

831
00:49:17,173 --> 00:49:19,976
That's my opinion
based on the investigation so far.

832
00:49:19,976 --> 00:49:21,177
What is that supposed to mean?

833
00:49:21,211 --> 00:49:23,012
If not sniping, then what?

834
00:49:26,483 --> 00:49:28,751
Pyo Gyu Cheol? Hey, he was shot to death.

835
00:49:29,152 --> 00:49:31,855
Kingfisher may have originally planned
to stage an accident,

836
00:49:31,888 --> 00:49:33,857
but an unforeseen variable arose,

837
00:49:33,857 --> 00:49:35,825
leading them to finish the job
with a sniper.

838
00:49:36,359 --> 00:49:37,360
What's your proof?

839
00:49:38,228 --> 00:49:39,662
(Analysis of Staged Accident Evidence)

840
00:49:39,662 --> 00:49:42,966
I selected eight high-level
child sex offenders,

841
00:49:42,999 --> 00:49:45,802
from the last 15 years,
since Kingfisher first appeared.

842
00:49:46,236 --> 00:49:47,437
All eight of them

843
00:49:47,771 --> 00:49:50,740
died in various accidents,
including car crashes,

844
00:49:50,740 --> 00:49:52,876
falls, electrocutions, and drownings.

845
00:49:53,910 --> 00:49:56,446
So while Kingfisher draws attention
with sniping,

846
00:49:56,913 --> 00:50:00,383
a separate team eliminates criminals
by staging various accidents?

847
00:50:03,086 --> 00:50:04,387
It's an interesting hypothesis.

848
00:50:05,588 --> 00:50:06,589
Hey.

849
00:50:07,257 --> 00:50:08,391
Inspector Yu, don't you start too.

850
00:50:10,126 --> 00:50:11,895
After tracking 20 criminals

851
00:50:11,895 --> 00:50:15,632
who received light sentences
and were released in the last 15 years,

852
00:50:15,932 --> 00:50:18,568
eleven of them were killed by Kingfisher,

853
00:50:19,002 --> 00:50:21,371
and eight died
in what were ruled as accidents.

854
00:50:21,938 --> 00:50:22,939
And...

855
00:50:23,973 --> 00:50:26,176
the most recent one to die
was Hwang Cheol Beom.

856
00:50:27,277 --> 00:50:30,246
He was so scared of Kingfisher,
so he went back to prison willingly,

857
00:50:30,246 --> 00:50:33,183
but we confirmed he died there last week.

858
00:50:33,183 --> 00:50:34,918
The cause of death was a heart attack.

859
00:50:35,785 --> 00:50:40,657
Oh, come on.
Accidental deaths, natural causes...

860
00:50:41,391 --> 00:50:43,393
It's not like
we're the dead-criminal squad.

861
00:50:43,393 --> 00:50:47,097
If 19 out of 20 are dead,
that means there's still 1 left.

862
00:50:48,665 --> 00:50:49,732
Who is it?

863
00:50:54,337 --> 00:50:55,572
Koo Jong Ryeol.

864
00:50:55,605 --> 00:50:58,708
About two years ago, a four-year-old boy

865
00:50:58,741 --> 00:51:02,011
<i>was brought to the ER</i>
<i>and died shortly after.</i>

866
00:51:02,779 --> 00:51:03,813
<i>You all remember that case, right?</i>

867
00:51:04,347 --> 00:51:06,049
<i>According to the medical records</i>
<i>at the time,</i>

868
00:51:06,049 --> 00:51:09,252
his abdomen was full of blood
from internal bleeding,

869
00:51:09,285 --> 00:51:10,787
and he had signs of broken bones
all over his body.

870
00:51:10,820 --> 00:51:13,456
The fractures all occurred
at different times.

871
00:51:13,456 --> 00:51:16,059
Gosh. What could they have done
to that child?

872
00:51:16,359 --> 00:51:17,560
The police investigation revealed

873
00:51:17,560 --> 00:51:20,363
that he was a victim
of horrific child abuse.

874
00:51:20,797 --> 00:51:22,532
The adoptive mother,
who was the main culprit, got nine years,

875
00:51:22,565 --> 00:51:25,401
and the biological father, Koo Jong Ryeol,
got two years for neglect.

876
00:51:25,735 --> 00:51:27,570
Neither of those sentences make any sense.

877
00:51:27,604 --> 00:51:29,139
The abuse was acknowledged,

878
00:51:29,172 --> 00:51:32,542
but they ruled there was
no criminal intent in the child's death,

879
00:51:32,542 --> 00:51:35,311
so they were charged
with involuntary manslaughter, not murder.

880
00:51:35,812 --> 00:51:38,181
Also, the boy's sister,
who was six at the time,

881
00:51:38,181 --> 00:51:39,883
gave testimony that favored her parents.

882
00:51:39,916 --> 00:51:41,985
Is there any chance
Koo Jong Ryeol really didn't know?

883
00:51:42,018 --> 00:51:44,220
The daughter later recanted her testimony.

884
00:51:44,254 --> 00:51:46,890
She said her father abused him too.

885
00:51:47,791 --> 00:51:51,261
But it wasn't accepted
because her statement was inconsistent.

886
00:51:52,395 --> 00:51:53,930
Where's the daughter now?

887
00:51:54,497 --> 00:51:57,300
Please tell me she's not with her father.

888
00:51:58,935 --> 00:52:00,303
She was removed from the home
after the incident

889
00:52:00,336 --> 00:52:01,905
and is now in a child protective facility.

890
00:52:01,938 --> 00:52:04,073
Mmm... That's a relief.

891
00:52:05,442 --> 00:52:06,443
So what about Koo Jong Ryeol?

892
00:52:06,476 --> 00:52:08,411
(The Only Survivor
Among The 20 Major Criminals)

893
00:52:08,445 --> 00:52:10,647
There's a high probability
he'll be Kingfisher's next target.

894
00:52:11,381 --> 00:52:12,415
That's my assessment.

895
00:52:12,882 --> 00:52:14,083
Who's taking this one?

896
00:52:14,083 --> 00:52:15,185
- I'll do it.
- I will...

897
00:52:20,790 --> 00:52:24,194
What's this?
Since when have you two been so in sync...

898
00:52:24,661 --> 00:52:25,862
as partners?

899
00:52:25,895 --> 00:52:28,098
As if.

900
00:52:28,098 --> 00:52:30,900
Right? Of course not. Not you two, right?

901
00:52:32,168 --> 00:52:35,138
Anyway, we need to lay low for a while,

902
00:52:35,171 --> 00:52:37,640
so the two of you can take this one.

903
00:52:37,640 --> 00:52:39,509
And Assistant Manager Ki,
make sure you back them up.

904
00:52:40,076 --> 00:52:41,144
Understood.

905
00:52:42,345 --> 00:52:44,147
<i>What? Use Koo Jong Ryeol?</i>

906
00:52:44,180 --> 00:52:46,182
Before Kingfisher makes a move,

907
00:52:46,216 --> 00:52:48,518
we'll set a trap around Koo Jong Ryeol...

908
00:52:48,518 --> 00:52:52,655
Are you suggesting we team up
with a criminal for a sting operation?

909
00:52:53,389 --> 00:52:54,758
I'm saying we should use this
as an opportunity.

910
00:52:55,258 --> 00:52:58,027
To be so sure
that Koo Jong Ryeol is the next target,

911
00:52:58,027 --> 00:52:59,295
the evidence seems pretty thin,
doesn't it?

912
00:53:00,029 --> 00:53:03,333
Right now, it's our only lead
to catch Kingfisher.

913
00:53:03,366 --> 00:53:06,169
But if you're right, Inspector Lee,

914
00:53:06,169 --> 00:53:08,905
there's no guarantee he'll use a sniper.

915
00:53:08,938 --> 00:53:11,274
How can we know when, where,
or how he'll strike...

916
00:53:11,274 --> 00:53:12,909
and just jump into this?

917
00:53:13,309 --> 00:53:15,912
Deploying equipment and personnel
based on a guess

918
00:53:16,613 --> 00:53:18,648
is like banging our heads against a wall.

919
00:53:19,549 --> 00:53:22,185
Team Leader, I believe we have
a good chance of success.

920
00:53:22,185 --> 00:53:24,921
- If you'll just hear me out...
- What else is there to hear?

921
00:53:25,922 --> 00:53:27,123
Team Leader.

922
00:53:29,325 --> 00:53:30,326
Go ahead.

923
00:53:31,928 --> 00:53:32,929
What?

924
00:53:34,464 --> 00:53:36,433
But you can't have any direct contact
with Koo Jong Ryeol.

925
00:53:37,033 --> 00:53:39,169
Does it make any sense
to work with a criminal...

926
00:53:39,169 --> 00:53:40,203
to catch another criminal?

927
00:53:40,970 --> 00:53:43,606
Second, I can't convince the higher-ups
without solid evidence.

928
00:53:44,007 --> 00:53:46,576
So I can't give you equipment
or manpower right now.

929
00:53:47,143 --> 00:53:49,345
Third, I can't give you unlimited time.

930
00:53:50,747 --> 00:53:52,248
For now, Inspector Lee,
you're on your own.

931
00:53:52,282 --> 00:53:54,851
Whether you two do a 24-hour stakeout
or surveillance...

932
00:53:54,884 --> 00:53:56,085
You have exactly one week.

933
00:53:56,085 --> 00:53:58,087
If you can get a lead on Kingfisher
within that time,

934
00:53:58,087 --> 00:53:59,889
I'll put my position
as Team Leader on the line...

935
00:53:59,923 --> 00:54:02,459
and get you all the support you want.
Got it?

936
00:54:03,460 --> 00:54:04,461
All right, meeting's over.

937
00:54:06,262 --> 00:54:08,965
Man, what a waste of time
this is going to be.

938
00:54:10,967 --> 00:54:12,035
Gosh, seriously.

939
00:54:12,635 --> 00:54:13,937
Let's go.

940
00:54:13,970 --> 00:54:15,872
(Phone Repair)

941
00:54:15,905 --> 00:54:17,040
Here you go.

942
00:54:21,644 --> 00:54:24,747
The audio files and all the other content
are still on here, right?

943
00:54:24,781 --> 00:54:28,051
Of course. We only replaced the battery,
so everything inside is still there.

944
00:54:40,130 --> 00:54:41,631
Mr. Ki already went downstairs.

945
00:55:10,093 --> 00:55:11,494
You always carry poisons.

946
00:55:11,528 --> 00:55:12,796
Of course.

947
00:55:13,263 --> 00:55:14,597
You're very guarded.

948
00:55:15,598 --> 00:55:16,833
Did you have an unhappy childhood?

949
00:55:17,233 --> 00:55:19,035
My childhood was plenty miserable.

950
00:55:19,035 --> 00:55:21,004
I've never even seen my parents' faces.

951
00:55:21,004 --> 00:55:22,372
That must have been nice.

952
00:55:22,372 --> 00:55:23,373
Not having a father.

953
00:55:23,840 --> 00:55:25,742
But you at least know
when you were born, right?

954
00:55:26,609 --> 00:55:27,744
I know the exact day.

955
00:55:28,178 --> 00:55:30,213
My ribs were broken on my fifth birthday.

956
00:55:40,890 --> 00:55:42,792
You can break bones without a father.

957
00:55:43,693 --> 00:55:44,694
Your arms, your legs.

958
00:56:09,185 --> 00:56:10,186
I'll be backup.

959
00:56:10,787 --> 00:56:11,788
Manager Yu.

960
00:56:13,757 --> 00:56:15,658
Are you really going to be our backup?

961
00:56:20,363 --> 00:56:21,831
Let's see what you two can do.

962
00:56:25,135 --> 00:56:26,402
You're going to drive too?

963
00:56:27,036 --> 00:56:28,104
Let's go, now.

964
00:56:29,105 --> 00:56:30,106
Get out.

965
00:56:36,246 --> 00:56:38,114
- Let's go.
- Okay.

966
00:56:47,557 --> 00:56:48,625
Keep a close eye on her.

967
00:56:49,392 --> 00:56:50,393
On what?

968
00:56:50,927 --> 00:56:51,928
Yu Bo Na.

969
00:56:52,495 --> 00:56:54,964
If you get a weird feeling,
we'll stop the Meeting immediately.

970
00:56:54,964 --> 00:56:55,999
Senior Bo Na?

971
00:56:58,301 --> 00:57:00,737
Is there something bothering you
about her?

972
00:57:01,638 --> 00:57:04,707
This client reminds me of someone.

973
00:57:07,177 --> 00:57:08,978
Certain memories from childhood...

974
00:57:10,146 --> 00:57:11,948
aren't easily erased.

975
00:57:21,482 --> 00:57:23,585
If he was going to approve it,
he should've just backed us all the way.

976
00:57:24,285 --> 00:57:26,588
This is neither an approval
nor a rejection.

977
00:57:28,423 --> 00:57:31,159
He could've at least assigned a few people
to relieve us on the stakeout.

978
00:57:37,465 --> 00:57:39,767
You seem to have a lot on your mind.

979
00:57:40,234 --> 00:57:42,870
Do you think there's any chance

980
00:57:43,371 --> 00:57:44,973
Kingfisher could be a woman?

981
00:57:45,273 --> 00:57:46,274
What?

982
00:57:49,877 --> 00:57:51,646
I'd say it's definitely possible, right?

983
00:57:55,049 --> 00:57:56,050
A foreigner?

984
00:57:56,784 --> 00:57:57,852
That seems possible too.

985
00:57:59,153 --> 00:58:00,154
A minor?

986
00:58:00,622 --> 00:58:01,823
There's no reason they couldn't be.

987
00:58:04,892 --> 00:58:05,893
Right.

988
00:58:07,562 --> 00:58:09,530
My gut tells me that behind Kingfisher,

989
00:58:09,530 --> 00:58:11,966
there's definitely a secret organization,
like a secret death squad.

990
00:58:12,634 --> 00:58:17,405
They live disguised as normal people,
and then when the order comes... bam!

991
00:58:18,039 --> 00:58:19,407
Just watch the road.

992
00:58:22,443 --> 00:58:23,745
I mean, for them to evade capture...

993
00:58:23,745 --> 00:58:25,580
after we've been investigating
for 15 years

994
00:58:25,580 --> 00:58:30,118
Don't you think they're disguised
as someone we'd never suspect?

995
00:59:10,992 --> 00:59:14,062
Being out in the field with you like this,
Manager Yu,

996
00:59:14,062 --> 00:59:15,063
is like a dream come true.

997
00:59:16,164 --> 00:59:17,932
I'm not here
to make your dreams come true.

998
00:59:18,766 --> 00:59:20,935
Hey, and next time, dream a little bigger.

999
00:59:22,837 --> 00:59:23,905
Okay.

1000
00:59:29,310 --> 00:59:31,145
But really, why are you here?

1001
00:59:31,813 --> 00:59:33,748
I heard you don't come to the field
for White.

1002
00:59:36,884 --> 00:59:38,920
I don't know,
it reminded me of the old days.

1003
00:59:44,292 --> 00:59:47,595
Manager Yu, can I ask who the Client was
for your first Meeting?

1004
00:59:48,363 --> 00:59:49,564
My first Meeting...

1005
00:59:54,402 --> 00:59:56,237
Well, who would that be?

1006
00:59:57,739 --> 00:59:58,806
What?

1007
01:00:04,412 --> 01:00:06,114
Okay, shall we get started?

1008
01:00:15,823 --> 01:00:17,392
Client Meeting is starting.

1009
01:00:53,962 --> 01:00:56,798
Wow, you were certainly busy
making a living.

1010
01:00:56,798 --> 01:01:01,703
Darn it, it dropped again.
These things are always tanking. Darn it.

1011
01:01:04,205 --> 01:01:06,040
Grip it tight.

1012
01:01:06,908 --> 01:01:08,643
Or you'll break another bone.

1013
01:01:12,213 --> 01:01:13,381
Darn it.

1014
01:01:17,218 --> 01:01:18,353
This is driving me nuts.

1015
01:01:31,599 --> 01:01:33,268
That crazy son of a gun.

1016
01:01:41,109 --> 01:01:42,277
Bo Na, don't.

1017
01:01:42,844 --> 01:01:43,845
Oh Hyun Nam.

1018
01:01:48,883 --> 01:01:50,251
(CCTV System)

1019
01:02:08,569 --> 01:02:11,105
(All Recordings)

1020
01:02:13,908 --> 01:02:16,678
(Call Recordings, Audio Files)

1021
01:02:19,147 --> 01:02:22,216
(Recording 2018-06-27)

1022
01:02:40,168 --> 01:02:42,670
You fell
because you don't have any patience,

1023
01:02:43,338 --> 01:02:46,374
but everyone thinks
that I was the one who did it.

1024
01:02:48,643 --> 01:02:50,645
They don't know how to raise tough kids.

1025
01:02:52,447 --> 01:02:54,449
What? Who are you people?

1026
01:03:02,357 --> 01:03:04,125
At King Tower,
in the fifth-floor emergency stairwell,

1027
01:03:04,125 --> 01:03:06,127
there's someone on the ground
bleeding from their head.

1028
01:03:08,029 --> 01:03:09,330
I think they're going to die
if you don't hurry.

1029
01:03:10,798 --> 01:03:13,034
<i>Because she could</i>
<i>have been a witness to Kingfisher,</i>

1030
01:03:13,601 --> 01:03:15,036
<i>or an accomplice.</i>

1031
01:03:23,144 --> 01:03:25,647
<i>Or she could be Kingfisher herself.</i>

1032
01:04:45,760 --> 01:04:49,897
(A Bona Fide Killer)

1033
01:04:49,931 --> 01:04:52,133
<i>Looks like you finally</i>
<i>opened the door.</i>

1034
01:04:52,734 --> 01:04:53,735
Tae Sung.

1035
01:04:53,768 --> 01:04:56,738
<i>Go with me or be abandoned.</i>

1036
01:04:56,738 --> 01:05:01,109
I'm just so curious; I have to ask.
And I need you to be honest with me.

1037
01:05:01,142 --> 01:05:03,278
Something unexpected must have come up
with your husband.

1038
01:05:03,311 --> 01:05:04,846
<i>If I go off somewhere again...</i>

1039
01:05:04,846 --> 01:05:05,847
<i>Where are you going?</i>

1040
01:05:05,847 --> 01:05:07,548
<i>The police network has been hacked.</i>

1041
01:05:07,548 --> 01:05:09,050
What if a member
of Kingfisher's organization

1042
01:05:09,050 --> 01:05:10,518
has infiltrated the police?

1043
01:05:10,551 --> 01:05:12,954
<i> This sister-in-law of yours,</i>
<i>what does she do?</i>

1044
01:05:13,554 --> 01:05:14,789
We have a witness.

1045
01:05:14,789 --> 01:05:18,793
<i>Could Kingfisher be a parent</i>
<i>raising a child?</i>

1046
01:05:18,793 --> 01:05:21,930
<i>The person you had to protect,</i>
<i>was it Kingfisher?</i>

1047
01:05:26,267 --> 01:05:29,070
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
